    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jue.2022.103528",
      "sequence": 5,
      "source_sequence": 5,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "JUE Insight: City-wide effects of new housing supply: Evidence from moving chains",
      "title_cn": "JUE洞察：新增住房供应的城市范围效应——来自搬迁链的证据",
      "authors": [
        "Cristina Bratu",
        "Oskari Harjunen",
        "Tuukka Saarimaa"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We study the city-wide effects of new, centrally-located market-rate housing supply using geo-coded population-wide register data from the Helsinki Metropolitan Area. The supply of new market rate units triggers moving chains that quickly reach middle- and low-income neighborhoods and individuals. Thus, new market-rate construction loosens the housing market in middle- and low-income areas even in the short run. Market-rate supply is likely to improve affordability outside the sub-markets where new construction occurs and to benefit low-income people.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们利用赫尔辛基大都会区的地理编码人口全覆盖登记数据，研究了位于市中心的新增市场价住房供应的城市范围效应。新增市场价单元供应触发的搬迁链迅速延伸至中低收入社区和个人。因此，即使在短期内，新增市场价建设也会松动中低收入地区的住房市场。市场价供应很可能改善新建区域以外子市场的可负担性，并使低收入人群受益。",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jue.2022.103528",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/journal-of-urban-economics/vol/133/suppl/C",
      "publication_date": "January 2023",
