    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jue.2022.103511",
      "sequence": 6,
      "source_sequence": 6,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "JUE Insight: Making it home? Evidence on the long-run impact of an intensive support program for the chronically homeless on housing, employment and health",
      "title_cn": "JUE Insight：能否回家？关于针对长期无家可归者的强化支持项目对住房、就业和健康的长期影响的证据",
      "authors": [
        "Daniel Kuehnle",
        "Guy Johnson",
        "Yi-Ping Tseng"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Interventions that combine unconditional permanent housing with support services, known as Housing First approaches, generally improve housing outcomes for people who have experienced chronic homelessness. However, little is known about their long-run outcomes or the consequences of ending such services. We investigate both aspects by examining the long-run effects of an intensive support program on the housing, employment, and health outcomes of chronically homeless people in Australia. Evaluating the three-year program over six-years using a randomised controlled trial , we document substantially higher rates of housing and better employment outcomes during the program period for the treated group, but no substantial changes in health. Three years after the program ends, we observe no significant differences between the treatment and control group with respect to any outcomes, including housing. Our results imply that stable housing is a necessary but not sufficient condition to overcome multiple sources of economic and social disadvantage.",
      "abstract_cn": "将无条件永久住房与支持服务相结合的干预措施，被称为“住房优先”方法，通常能改善经历过长期无家可归者的住房结果。然而，关于其长期结果或终止此类服务的后果，人们知之甚少。我们通过考察一个强化支持项目对澳大利亚长期无家可归者在住房、就业和健康结果方面的长期影响，对这两个方面进行了研究。我们使用随机对照试验对一个为期三年的项目进行了为期六年的评估，记录了在项目期间接受治疗组在住房率和就业结果方面显著更高，但在健康方面没有实质性变化。项目结束三年后，我们观察到治疗组和对照组在任何结果上，包括住房方面，都没有显著差异。我们的结果表明，稳定住房是克服多种经济和社会劣势来源的必要但不充分条件。",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jue.2022.103511",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/journal-of-urban-economics/vol/133/suppl/C",
      "publication_date": "January 2023",
