    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jue.2021.103393",
      "sequence": 11,
      "source_sequence": 11,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "JUE Insight: Zoning and property taxation revisited—Was Hamilton right?",
      "title_cn": "JUE洞察：分区与财产税再探讨——汉密尔顿是对的吗？",
      "authors": [
        "Jan K. Brueckner"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "In rare theoretical treatments of ideas developed by Hamilton (1975, 1976) almost fifty wears ago, recent papers by Barseghyan and Coate (2016) and Calabrese et al. (2007) develop dynamic models to analyze zoning and property taxation in a system of communities. Their analyses led to negative conclusions, contradicting Hamilton’s view, by showing that efficient zoning does not emerge in equilibrium. The purpose of this note is to show that a different, affirmative conclusion can be reached in a simpler, highly stylized model that formalizes Hamilton’s idea.",
      "abstract_cn": "在近五十年前汉密尔顿（1975，1976）提出的思想的罕见理论处理中，Barseghyan和Coate（2016）以及Calabrese等人（2007）的最新论文开发了动态模型来分析社区体系中的分区和财产税。他们的分析得出了负面结论，与汉密尔顿的观点相矛盾，表明有效分区不会在均衡中出现。本文的目的是表明，在一个更简单、高度风格化的模型中，可以得出不同的、肯定的结论，该模型形式化了汉密尔顿的思想。",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jue.2021.103393",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/journal/journal-of-urban-economics/vol/133/suppl/C",
      "publication_date": "January 2023",
